1
00:00:14,060 --> 00:00:18,420
Aiming for the sunset
floating over the Nakagawa,

2
00:00:18,420 --> 00:00:23,900
kicking a pebble, I leap along.

3
00:00:24,480 --> 00:00:29,360
To Kashiwa, the type who was out jogging,

4
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:33,800
they laughed that I stayed
just as cheerful as ever.

5
00:00:33,800 --> 00:00:37,440
Even if I somehow stir up some energy,

6
00:00:37,440 --> 00:00:38,700
Gutsy, there's a reason for it.

7
00:00:38,700 --> 00:00:41,040
One nightmare that never changes.

8
00:00:41,040 --> 00:00:43,880
The streets are kinder somehow.

9
00:00:44,680 --> 00:00:47,020
Because the crows are cawing,

10
00:00:47,020 --> 00:00:48,720
the sun has already gone down.

11
00:00:49,820 --> 00:00:51,940
Stuffing yakitori in my cheeks.

12
00:00:51,940 --> 00:00:53,860
Will you see it?

13
00:00:54,860 --> 00:00:57,500
Of the pointed hat,

14
00:00:57,500 --> 00:01:04,060
from over there toward Daishaku-den,
the sunset falls.

15
00:01:06,780 --> 00:01:10,080
Tomorrow too, it'll end in a drop, won't it?

16
00:01:10,080 --> 00:01:13,660
Again, even happiness gets lost.

17
00:01:13,660 --> 00:01:16,300
Because I'm a fool who finally realized it.

18
00:01:17,040 --> 00:01:17,600
Yeah

19
00:01:25,140 --> 00:01:27,120
The Inventor King, Ryotsu

20
00:01:29,800 --> 00:01:33,560
Sauce, soy sauce, sauce, soy sauce

21
00:01:33,560 --> 00:01:35,620
No matter what anyone says, it's sauce.

22
00:01:35,620 --> 00:01:38,100
You're talking nonsense. It's soy sauce.

23
00:01:38,100 --> 00:01:39,360
Good morning, Kankichi.

24
00:01:39,360 --> 00:01:42,520
What's all this noise
first thing in the morning?

25
00:01:42,520 --> 00:01:45,840
It's about what to put on fried eggs.

26
00:01:48,600 --> 00:01:49,680
Really, it should be sauce, right?

27
00:01:49,680 --> 00:01:52,240
Anyone from the police box uses soy sauce.

28
00:01:52,780 --> 00:01:54,080
I use salt, though.

29
00:01:54,080 --> 00:01:55,420
As for lemon,

30
00:01:55,420 --> 00:01:56,300
it's sauce, then.

31
00:01:57,620 --> 00:01:58,560
It's soy sauce, obviously.

32
00:01:58,560 --> 00:01:59,960
I don't put anything on them.

33
00:01:59,960 --> 00:02:03,020
Savoring them as they are is the best way.

34
00:02:03,020 --> 00:02:05,580
So it's settled, then. Soy sauce.

35
00:02:05,580 --> 00:02:07,080
It's not settled.

36
00:02:08,020 --> 00:02:10,760
Then put soy sauce on my fried egg.

37
00:02:11,200 --> 00:02:13,160
Here, I am the law.

38
00:02:13,160 --> 00:02:16,740
It's been decided since long
ago that fried eggs get sauce.

39
00:02:19,920 --> 00:02:20,860
Kankichi!

40
00:02:22,200 --> 00:02:26,440
It's not like we have to go to that super easy sushi place.
There are other places to eat.

41
00:02:27,080 --> 00:02:28,580
Is Ryotsu not here?

42
00:02:29,140 --> 00:02:30,220
Late again

43
00:02:30,220 --> 00:02:31,460
He's hopeless.

44
00:02:31,460 --> 00:02:33,680
When he shows up,
I'll give him a good scolding.

45
00:02:33,680 --> 00:02:36,540
Damn it,
I can't get near the police box like this.

46
00:02:39,620 --> 00:02:41,900
My bicycle and my stomach
are in perfect harmony.

47
00:02:41,900 --> 00:02:44,460
Ryo's diner should have something, right?

48
00:02:46,900 --> 00:02:48,280
W-what's going on?

49
00:02:48,820 --> 00:02:49,880
Ryo-san.

50
00:02:49,880 --> 00:02:51,860
What's going on?

51
00:02:51,860 --> 00:02:54,300
They said Ryo's construction starts today.

52
00:02:54,300 --> 00:02:57,240
It's been posted on the bulletin board for a month,
you know.

53
00:02:57,240 --> 00:02:59,200
I-I didn't know.

54
00:03:00,120 --> 00:03:02,980
I've already put Ryo-san's
things out over there.

55
00:03:04,420 --> 00:03:06,500
They'll take it for trash!

56
00:03:06,500 --> 00:03:09,180
It's fine, I wrote a name on it.

57
00:03:09,180 --> 00:03:10,680
That's not what I mean,

58
00:03:11,580 --> 00:03:13,700
what happened to the food
that was in the canteen?

59
00:03:14,040 --> 00:03:15,220
Isn't there anything left?

60
00:03:15,220 --> 00:03:17,620
We finished it all up yesterday.

61
00:03:18,760 --> 00:03:20,240
I'm going on a trip now,

62
00:03:20,240 --> 00:03:21,780
see you, Ryo-san.

63
00:03:21,780 --> 00:03:23,560
Wait a second!

64
00:03:23,560 --> 00:03:25,200
What's food?

65
00:03:25,200 --> 00:03:27,540
I ended up saying that.

66
00:03:29,480 --> 00:03:30,640
I'm starving.

67
00:03:33,000 --> 00:03:35,600
I'm starving,
the bicycle's going to burn too.

68
00:03:40,840 --> 00:03:41,860
It's narutomaki.

69
00:03:42,680 --> 00:03:45,580
Even so, you shouldn't be
eating things off the ground.

70
00:03:45,580 --> 00:03:46,520
As a human being,

71
00:03:46,520 --> 00:03:49,400
Hey, but Semihara isn't going home, is he?

72
00:03:49,400 --> 00:03:50,480
Nyan.

73
00:03:50,480 --> 00:03:54,060
Hey, hey! Th-that's someone else's food!

74
00:03:54,060 --> 00:03:56,780
Damn it, I don't have time to hesitate!

75
00:03:57,680 --> 00:03:58,620
Excuse me, coming in.

76
00:03:58,620 --> 00:04:00,300
Welcome.

77
00:04:00,720 --> 00:04:01,420
Is Kankichi here?

78
00:04:01,820 --> 00:04:02,980
If it's Ryo-chan,

79
00:04:02,980 --> 00:04:05,520
he's been absent without leave
from here for a while now, but

80
00:04:05,520 --> 00:04:07,280
he isn't here either, is he?

81
00:04:07,280 --> 00:04:11,020
Isn't he working at Cho-Kande Sushi?

82
00:04:11,560 --> 00:04:14,200
He does that lately whenever
he runs out of money.

83
00:04:14,200 --> 00:04:17,480
Yesterday he got into a fight
with Grandma and stormed out.

84
00:04:17,480 --> 00:04:19,380
Lemon is worried, you know.

85
00:04:19,380 --> 00:04:22,680
We've searched everywhere,
but we just can't find him.

86
00:04:22,680 --> 00:04:26,820
It's Ryo-chan, so I think he'll
be fine no matter what happens, but

87
00:04:27,260 --> 00:04:28,880
I'm a little worried, though.

88
00:04:29,260 --> 00:04:31,160
We have no choice but
to use our last resort.

89
00:04:38,600 --> 00:04:39,680
I'm starving.

90
00:04:41,940 --> 00:04:44,980
When you're hungry,
the autumn wind cuts right to the bone.

91
00:04:48,200 --> 00:04:49,420
W-wh-what the...?

92
00:04:49,420 --> 00:04:50,780
Brrr!

93
00:04:52,240 --> 00:04:53,360
That car...

94
00:04:53,360 --> 00:04:54,300
What a coincidence.

95
00:04:54,300 --> 00:04:55,900
Running into you here like this,

96
00:04:55,900 --> 00:04:57,020
so it really is you.

97
00:04:57,020 --> 00:04:59,640
You flew a helicopter to the
park and call it a coincidence?

98
00:05:01,220 --> 00:05:04,120
So you traced my PHS, didn't you?

99
00:05:04,120 --> 00:05:05,260
Who asked you to do this?

100
00:05:05,260 --> 00:05:06,120
Was it the Chief?

101
00:05:06,120 --> 00:05:07,360
No, not really.

102
00:05:07,360 --> 00:05:09,400
It's not because someone asked me to,

103
00:05:09,680 --> 00:05:10,840
it really was just a coincidence.

104
00:05:11,420 --> 00:05:12,780
Y-yeah, that's right.

105
00:05:12,780 --> 00:05:15,620
I wasn't searching for him because
Lemon-san asked me to or anything.

106
00:05:16,020 --> 00:05:17,540
Lemon

107
00:05:18,900 --> 00:05:20,200
A-anyway,

108
00:05:20,200 --> 00:05:23,180
we're about to throw a
home party at my place.

109
00:05:23,180 --> 00:05:26,280
Why don't you come too?
There's plenty of food.

110
00:05:26,780 --> 00:05:31,140
It's not like Lemon-san asked me to
get you to eat a meal or anything.

111
00:05:31,140 --> 00:05:35,200
Okay, okay, I don't care about the reason.
Let's hurry and go!

112
00:05:36,600 --> 00:05:38,060
I've reached my limit.

113
00:05:39,680 --> 00:05:41,940
I ate, I ate! I'm back from the dead!

114
00:05:43,560 --> 00:05:46,080
I'm glad to hear it. Please clean up.

115
00:05:52,200 --> 00:05:52,540
What is this?

116
00:05:56,600 --> 00:05:59,720
So you don't even have to tidy up yourself

117
00:06:00,180 --> 00:06:02,340
Same old high-tech house

118
00:06:02,440 --> 00:06:04,440
Just snap your fingers and
the machines start moving.

119
00:06:04,580 --> 00:06:05,780
Alright, I'll give it a try too.

120
00:06:06,580 --> 00:06:08,180
TV, turn on!

121
00:06:09,680 --> 00:06:10,760
Is it broken?

122
00:06:11,120 --> 00:06:12,920
It's registered to the
sound of your finger snap.

123
00:06:13,440 --> 00:06:15,800
It doesn't respond to anyone
else's finger snap but mine.

124
00:06:16,760 --> 00:06:17,440
TV

125
00:06:20,080 --> 00:06:22,420
Maybe it's broken after all?

126
00:06:22,660 --> 00:06:24,080
That can't be right.

127
00:06:25,620 --> 00:06:26,460
Yeah, it's broken.

128
00:06:26,460 --> 00:06:28,220
TV, TV!

129
00:06:30,080 --> 00:06:31,740
What's going on with this TV?

130
00:06:31,740 --> 00:06:33,500
I told you, it's broken.

131
00:06:33,500 --> 00:06:34,440
There's no other way.

132
00:06:34,440 --> 00:06:36,840
In that case, I'll use the ultimate remote.

133
00:06:36,840 --> 00:06:38,740
The ultimate remote?

134
00:06:39,680 --> 00:06:40,760
Switch on!

135
00:06:41,460 --> 00:06:43,780
Isn't this just a stick?

136
00:06:43,780 --> 00:06:45,480
Here's the next news.

137
00:06:45,480 --> 00:06:47,440
At Super Electronics Machinery,

138
00:06:47,440 --> 00:06:49,620
Isn't this your company?

139
00:06:49,620 --> 00:06:50,040
Yeah.

140
00:06:50,040 --> 00:06:52,600
At Super Electronics Machinery,

141
00:06:52,600 --> 00:06:55,360
a portion of the sales of products
that have been commercialized

142
00:06:55,360 --> 00:06:58,500
will be paid to the developers as a reward,
they announced.

143
00:06:59,440 --> 00:07:01,480
What? Is this really true?

144
00:07:01,480 --> 00:07:03,240
Why would they lie?

145
00:07:03,540 --> 00:07:05,800
How much of a portion of the sales is it?

146
00:07:06,080 --> 00:07:08,420
It depends on the sales amount, though.

147
00:07:09,680 --> 00:07:12,200
If it were developed,
I'd be willing to pay out 10 billion

148
00:07:12,200 --> 00:07:16,780
10 billion means 10 billion yen

149
00:07:16,780 --> 00:07:17,300
Yeah.

150
00:07:17,300 --> 00:07:18,780
10 billion yen.

151
00:07:18,780 --> 00:07:22,840
With 10 billion,
I'd never have to go hungry again.

152
00:07:22,840 --> 00:07:24,460
Let me have a go too.

153
00:07:24,460 --> 00:07:24,860
What?

154
00:07:25,340 --> 00:07:27,620
I've got an idea for a huge hit product.

155
00:07:28,660 --> 00:07:29,220
Done.

156
00:07:29,900 --> 00:07:30,960
Already done?

157
00:07:31,080 --> 00:07:31,473
Yeah,

158
00:07:31,523 --> 00:07:35,220
I call it the Safety Box Printabra Ranger.

159
00:07:35,900 --> 00:07:36,620
What is this?

160
00:07:36,620 --> 00:07:42,880
You've surely had your pudding in the
fridge eaten by your siblings, right?

161
00:07:42,880 --> 00:07:46,880
Often, that leads to a fight
between brothers and sisters.

162
00:07:46,880 --> 00:07:49,020
And this is what solves that problem.

163
00:07:49,020 --> 00:07:51,480
It won't open unless you enter the code.

164
00:07:51,480 --> 00:07:55,680
The pudding is fully protected and there are no more sibling fights.
Two birds with one stone!

165
00:07:55,680 --> 00:08:00,660
Press the registered number and it opens like this.
It's a great invention, right?

166
00:08:00,660 --> 00:08:02,040
Who would buy that?

167
00:08:02,040 --> 00:08:06,220
Only a household with lots of siblings
and enough money to buy pudding.

168
00:08:06,220 --> 00:08:10,200
With the falling birth rate, households
with siblings are getting fewer every year.

169
00:08:10,200 --> 00:08:12,660
Besides, how much did the materials cost?

170
00:08:12,660 --> 00:08:14,760
Cheap, under 100,000 yen.

171
00:08:14,760 --> 00:08:19,460
How many houses would spend that much
money for a 100 or 200 yen pudding?

172
00:08:19,460 --> 00:08:21,500
Though there are probably
at least a hundred.

173
00:08:22,280 --> 00:08:23,340
This is hopeless.

174
00:08:23,340 --> 00:08:25,900
Wait, wait! I have plenty of other ideas.

175
00:08:25,900 --> 00:08:27,440
You can count on the next one!

176
00:08:27,980 --> 00:08:31,680
Next is this: the Safety Box Marenger.

177
00:08:32,040 --> 00:08:38,540
Boo! It's the same as the last one.
Anyone can open it faster now, can't they?

178
00:08:39,540 --> 00:08:49,340
I'll show you real product development, not this nonsense.
This is what product development looks like: the ultra-small battery we're developing right here.

179
00:08:49,980 --> 00:08:56,500
If this is completed, every battery-powered device will be miniaturized,
and a battery revolution will happen.

180
00:08:57,200 --> 00:08:59,820
Of course, the sales will be enormous.

181
00:08:59,820 --> 00:09:01,500
This is a product that will sell.

182
00:09:01,500 --> 00:09:01,960
I see.

183
00:09:03,240 --> 00:09:05,280
Of course, development takes time too.

184
00:09:05,280 --> 00:09:07,340
It's not something you can do on the side.

185
00:09:07,800 --> 00:09:08,480
Yeah, that's right.

186
00:09:08,480 --> 00:09:11,080
Now that you understand,
go back home quietly.

187
00:09:11,080 --> 00:09:14,880
From now on,
I'll stay here and develop products.

188
00:09:15,800 --> 00:09:18,920
Don't worry,
I'll develop a product that will amaze you.

189
00:09:23,200 --> 00:09:25,120
Then I'll lend you this room.

190
00:09:26,500 --> 00:09:30,500
If I lock him in this warehouse, he won't be
able to get in the way of our company people.

191
00:09:30,500 --> 00:09:32,100
What's this?

192
00:09:32,760 --> 00:09:34,520
It's a talking translation robot.

193
00:09:34,520 --> 00:09:36,840
A talking translation robot?

194
00:09:37,160 --> 00:09:38,791
When you speak to it in Japanese,

195
00:09:38,841 --> 00:09:41,440
it automatically translates
into English and speaks it out.

196
00:09:41,440 --> 00:09:43,700
It can also turn English into Japanese.

197
00:09:43,700 --> 00:09:44,120
Is that so?

198
00:09:44,460 --> 00:09:47,068
In theory, it should be correct,

199
00:09:47,118 --> 00:09:49,620
but it didn't work out,
so development was cancelled.

200
00:09:49,620 --> 00:09:50,700
What a waste.

201
00:09:50,700 --> 00:09:54,060
If we finish this, do we get a bonus?

202
00:09:54,780 --> 00:09:55,900
If we can finish it, sure.

203
00:09:57,500 --> 00:09:58,180
Alright then!

204
00:10:01,160 --> 00:10:02,380
The build is rough, isn't it.

205
00:10:02,380 --> 00:10:05,000
It must have been made by
someone clumsy with their hands.

206
00:10:05,000 --> 00:10:08,180
Anyway, with the skills I
built up making plastic models,

207
00:10:08,180 --> 00:10:10,580
I reassembled it
following the blueprint, but

208
00:10:10,580 --> 00:10:11,860
Yes, it's done!

209
00:10:11,860 --> 00:10:13,860
This must be the switch.

210
00:10:14,440 --> 00:10:16,440
I'm exhausted and sleepy.

211
00:10:17,500 --> 00:10:18,560
I'm sleepy

212
00:10:20,160 --> 00:10:22,240
Didn't this thing just talk?

213
00:10:23,140 --> 00:10:25,840
My name is Kankichi Ryotsu.

214
00:10:27,500 --> 00:10:28,340
March 4th

215
00:10:28,340 --> 00:10:30,980
W-wait, isn't this already finished?

216
00:10:31,720 --> 00:10:35,240
Yay! I'm going to be a millionaire!

217
00:10:35,680 --> 00:10:38,520
I got it! I can be a millionaire!

218
00:10:39,140 --> 00:10:39,960
Mm-hmm, mm-hmm.

219
00:10:39,960 --> 00:10:42,320
Wait a minute.

220
00:10:42,320 --> 00:10:45,560
Whether this thing is
really translating correctly

221
00:10:45,560 --> 00:10:47,160
I can't judge that on my own.

222
00:10:47,160 --> 00:10:49,400
Guess I'll have those guys check it.

223
00:11:24,680 --> 00:11:27,480
BGM

224
00:11:27,500 --> 00:11:30,200
It's a talking translator.
Is the English right?

225
00:11:30,420 --> 00:11:31,400
Spot on.

226
00:11:31,620 --> 00:11:33,960
Alright, next is English to Japanese.

227
00:11:34,260 --> 00:11:35,300
Let me do it.

228
00:11:35,840 --> 00:11:38,340
Sure, go ahead. The super tie is the switch.

229
00:11:38,660 --> 00:11:39,300
This one, right?

230
00:11:39,740 --> 00:11:41,260
How about green tea?

231
00:11:41,520 --> 00:11:42,940
Would you like some green tea?

232
00:11:43,560 --> 00:11:44,620
It's correct.

233
00:11:45,340 --> 00:11:47,821
A perfect talking translator,

234
00:11:47,871 --> 00:11:49,360
is probably a world first.

235
00:11:49,740 --> 00:11:52,000
It's a world-class invention, senpai.

236
00:11:52,380 --> 00:11:53,440
I see.

237
00:11:54,180 --> 00:11:54,580
Alright.

238
00:11:55,240 --> 00:11:56,340
Chief.

239
00:11:57,500 --> 00:11:59,180
Where were you and what
were you doing until now?

240
00:11:59,180 --> 00:12:01,540
Well, it's a long story.

241
00:12:01,540 --> 00:12:04,040
This time, my patience has finally snapped.

242
00:12:04,040 --> 00:12:05,920
Kneel down right there!

243
00:12:05,920 --> 00:12:07,040
Wait, please.

244
00:12:07,040 --> 00:12:09,540
I've made a genuine great invention, I have!

245
00:12:09,540 --> 00:12:11,500
Don't talk nonsense.

246
00:12:11,500 --> 00:12:12,620
I'm telling you, it's the truth.

247
00:12:13,240 --> 00:12:14,040
What is this?

248
00:12:14,040 --> 00:12:15,080
What is this

249
00:12:15,080 --> 00:12:16,800
It talked!

250
00:12:17,260 --> 00:12:19,200
This is a talking translation robot.

251
00:12:19,200 --> 00:12:21,320
A perfect talking translation machine

252
00:12:21,320 --> 00:12:23,880
hasn't been successfully developed yet.

253
00:12:23,880 --> 00:12:26,540
It's truly a groundbreaking invention!

254
00:12:29,240 --> 00:12:31,120
Yes. This is a world-class...

255
00:12:32,400 --> 00:12:34,352
Right. Speaking of world-class, tomorrow,

256
00:12:34,402 --> 00:12:38,140
there's a party for police
officials from around the world.

257
00:12:38,480 --> 00:12:40,435
The chief and I are invited too.

258
00:12:40,485 --> 00:12:42,800
I'll take you along, too.

259
00:12:43,320 --> 00:12:43,680
Right?

260
00:12:44,140 --> 00:12:46,640
That's where we'll unveil
that translation machine.

261
00:12:46,840 --> 00:12:48,960
People all over the world
are sure to be amazed.

262
00:12:49,460 --> 00:12:51,700
You'll become a world-famous
celebrity overnight!

263
00:12:52,240 --> 00:12:53,900
A world-famous celebrity

264
00:12:58,280 --> 00:12:59,280
